Article 33
The form of service as referred to in Article 26 (1) paragraph (1), shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.
The Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1) (2) constitutes Regional Apparatus that implements duties and functions in the field of:
a. women's empowerment and child protection; b. social affairs;
c. manpower;
d. health;
e. education;
f. security and public order; and
g. mental and spiritual.
In implementing the duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Apparatus may (3) cooperate with government agencies, provincial government, other district/city governments and the community as well as the business sector.
